speechtext:
I shall be glad to do so:
Where, irrespective of such facts, the principle is objectionable, the house will not consent to the second reading;
I think there has been a confusion in the thinking of hon. members opposite. Perhaps I am doing them an injustice. I know there are members in the house who in principle will not vote for a divorce bill because they disapprove of divorce as such, as a matter of conscience. That is one thing, but what is cited in the rule I have just read is a wholly different thing. What is in the rule here is the principle of granting divorce in itself.
